{"version":"1","id":"planetscale","handle":"planetscale","name":"PlanetScale","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/09515c29cafc45618b3f117eab4fccf8","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-8.6678,"y":0.7142,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":154,"newest_post_at":"2026-04-24T16:27:04.053Z","oldest_post_at":"2022-11-18T16:00:25.238Z","features":{"hype_score":0.006536,"listicle_ratio":0.0,"question_ratio":0.058824,"avg_read_time":6.479452,"summary_length_avg":331.143836,"title_length_avg":49.529412,"title_length_var":1280.549789,"tag_entropy":3.186211,"tag_diversity":0.571429,"top_tag_share":0.37013,"avg_upvotes":6.480519,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.142857,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.023023,"zero_engagement_share":0.233766,"viral_share":0.006494,"posts_per_week":0.860322,"non_article_ratio":0.064935,"author_present_share":0.064935,"recency_skew":0.069444},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[5.6912,-2.3529],"cadence_depth":[1.7353,1.2647],"hype_variety":[-0.4706,0.0],"title_style":[6.5735,-0.8824]},"top_tags":[["database",88],["mysql",71],["planetscale",66],["backend",21],["performance",19],["postgresql",16],["devops",11],["aws",10]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Database Sharding \u2014 PlanetScale","B-trees and database indexes","Pagination in MySQL"],"outlier":["pgcopydb is the best way to migrate to PlanetScale Postgres.\n\nWe've used it to move multi-TB databases at speeds over 2 TB/hr.\n\nPlanetScale's custom fork adds PG 17/18 support, better CDC, and resilient retry. Check out our new migration guide!"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"RyXFZf9TY","title":"Multi-tenancy is a term used across various kinds of technical infrastructure, including application hosting, compute, and databases. In this article, we use a single Postgres database cluster to serve an application with many tenants.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/multi-tenancy-is-a-term-used-across-various-kinds-of-technical-infrastructure-including-application-ryxfzf9ty","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--CxzD6vbw--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2005","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T16:27:04.053Z"},{"id":"UnQpiaK3O","title":"View the complete distribution of tags assigned to a query pattern, search queries by tag, and see a per-tag breakdown of database-level statistics","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/view-the-complete-distribution-of-tags-assigned-to-a-query-pattern-search-queries-by-tag-and-see-a-unqpiak3o","summary":"PlanetScale has enhanced its Insights query tagging feature for Postgres databases as part of the Traffic Control launch. Tags are now present in aggregated query data rather than only on individual notable query logs. This enables viewing the complete distribution of tags assigned to a query pattern, searching queries by tag, and seeing per-tag breakdowns of database-level statistics. The post covers both a feature overview and implementation details.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--pkAJWVyz--/f_auto/v1776701854/posts/UnQpiaK3O?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-20T16:17:34.225Z"},{"id":"hoQTYuD80","title":"Core Flow AI builds AI-powered entertainment apps. This involves everything from the web app to the infrastructure and all the AI models. They are responsible for a top 50 gen AI consumer app with over 500k users a day.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/core-flow-ai-builds-ai-powered-entertainment-apps-this-involves-everything-from-the-web-app-to-the--hoqtyud80","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-16T17:05:45.927Z"},{"id":"H4d9Mtxvk","title":"pgcopydb is the best way to migrate to PlanetScale Postgres.\n\nWe've used it to move multi-TB databases at speeds over 2 TB/hr.\n\nPlanetScale's custom fork adds PG 17/18 support, better CDC, and resilient retry. Check out our new migration guide!","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/pgcopydb-is-the-best-way-to-migrate-to-planetscale-postgres-we-ve-used-it-to-move-multi-tb-databas-h4d9mtxvk","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--58gMhC4P--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2012","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-15T15:33:59.663Z"},{"id":"Q07NqKrL0","title":"Cash App's move to PlanetScale resulted in streamlined database operations, improved performance, and reduced operational overhead.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/cash-app-s-move-to-planetscale-resulted-in-streamlined-database-operations-improved-performance-an-q07nqkrl0","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-14T16:13:42.535Z"},{"id":"FxiDqsL0u","title":"Let's dig into what PlanetScale's Traffic Control looks like in your codebase!","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/let-s-dig-into-what-planetscale-s-traffic-control-looks-like-in-your-codebase--fxidqsl0u","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--2-1xRawN--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2011","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-13T16:46:22.731Z"},{"id":"BnDAeYlHb","title":"It's now possible to view the complete distribution of tags assigned to a query pattern, search queries by tag, and see a per-tag breakdown of database-level statistics.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/it-s-now-possible-to-view-the-complete-distribution-of-tags-assigned-to-a-query-pattern-search-quer-bndaeylhb","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--HRgLpUt6--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2003","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-09T19:12:38.576Z"},{"id":"Og8vNgS5F","title":"We're excited to announce that PlanetScale is participating as a co-design and launch partner for Stripe Projects, a new developer preview from Stripe that centralizes dev tool provisioning and billing in one place.","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/we-re-excited-to-announce-that-planetscale-is-participating-as-a-co-design-and-launch-partner-for-st-og8vngs5f","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--OHB84bZF--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2010","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-07T15:12:09.686Z"},{"id":"iiYw9ngNw","title":null,"url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/iiyw9ngnw","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--1KxV4ohY--/f_auto/v1722860400/public/Placeholder%2007","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-02T14:58:54.983Z"},{"id":"ifSg0VRzh","title":"Graceful degradation in Postgres","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/graceful-degradation-in-postgres-ifsg0vrzh","summary":"PlanetScale's Traffic Control feature introduces resource budgets for PostgreSQL, enabling graceful degradation under load. By applying strict limits to different traffic slices, high-priority queries are protected even during request surges, preventing total database outages.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ajeoUtsv--/f_auto/v1775078683/posts/ifSg0VRzh?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-01T21:24:43.448Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"wPYPVCTAb","title":"Database Sharding \u2014 PlanetScale","url":"https://planetscale.com/blog/database-sharding","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/database-sharding-planetscale-wpypvctab","summary":"Sharding is the process of improving database scalability by distributing data across multiple servers, known as shards. This technique is widely used by large companies like Uber and Slack. Effective sharding involves choosing the right sharding strategy and shard key to optimize performance and avoid issues like cross-shard queries. PlanetScale, built on Vitess, provides tools to simplify sharding implementation and management. Additionally, sharding can help with data durability, high availability, and faster backups by using replicas.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c1d452d1d38c78b63c23005b6295bd54?_a=AQAEuj9","num_upvotes":109,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-09T16:43:18.038Z"},{"id":"gvsPlIcyu","title":"B-trees and database indexes","url":"https://planetscale.com/blog/btrees-and-database-indexes","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/b-trees-and-database-indexes-gvsplicyu","summary":"B-trees and B+ trees are essential for efficient data lookups in database management systems like MySQL, Postgres, and MongoDB. They are structured to store key/value pairs in a way that optimizes search operations. MySQL's InnoDB engine relies heavily on B+ trees, where the choice of primary key significantly impacts performance. B-trees are well-suited for large data volumes that need persistent disk storage, and B+ trees offer advantages like storing all values at the leaf level and having linked lists for faster sequential access. Sequential keys generally improve performance over random or UUID keys.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/a8db96bd9345cbfd2319bb8253d31107?_a=AQAEuiZ","num_upvotes":99,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2024-09-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"gSub4SQnv","title":"Pagination in MySQL","url":"https://planetscale.com/blog/mysql-pagination","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/pagination-in-mysql-gsub4sqnv","summary":"There are two primary ways to paginate in MySQL: offset/limit and cursors. If you sort your rows by a column that is not unique, MySQL gets to decide which order to return these rows in. The easiest way to produce deterministic ordering is to order by a unique column because every value will be distinct.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1681835116/fa21263ff103ce4b70594d94093c000b","num_upvotes":68,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2023-04-18T00:03:57.000Z"},{"id":"vUy9ChOpx","title":"Announcing Neki \u2014 PlanetScale","url":"https://planetscale.com/blog/announcing-neki","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-neki-planetscale-vuy9chopx","summary":"PlanetScale announces Neki, a new sharded Postgres solution built from first principles by the team behind Vitess. Unlike Vitess which leverages MySQL, Neki is designed specifically for Postgres workloads and will be released as open source when ready. The project aims to bring the same extreme scale capabilities that Vitess provides for MySQL to the Postgres ecosystem.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2271e3372fcd54b9756cebec470ed6de?_a=AQAEulh","num_upvotes":51,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-08-11T18:47:02.115Z"},{"id":"GgbRsSWoV","title":"Introducing the Issues Calendar for GitHub Projects","url":"https://planetscale.com/blog/introducing-the-issues-calendar-for-github-projects","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-the-issues-calendar-for-github-projects-ggbrsswov","summary":"Introducing the Issues Calendar for GitHub Projects, an open-source tool that allows users to view GitHub project issues in a customizable calendar. The tool integrates with GitHub's OAuth system, allowing users to sign in with their existing credentials and import projects they have access to. Any issue with a due date assigned will be displayed on the calendar.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/62b6ecd94decdb7a8a2fce7b6e979cd4?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":29,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2023-03-15T15:39:36.603Z"}],"similar_handles":["awsplainenglish","microservicesio","rustlib","tia","codrops"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","ham